-- title:
--   Uniform q^m-index bound on the localised Eisenstein quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and suppose `HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar p` holds, i.e. the operators $\bar T_\ell$ on $J_0(p) =$ `JZero p` $= \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ commute pairwise; this gives `JZero p` a module structure over $\mathbb T =$ `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$. Let $q$ be a prime. Write $\widetilde J =$ `EisensteinQuotient p` for the quotient of `JZero p` by the submodule $\mathrm{eisensteinKernel}\cdot\top$ attached to the Eisenstein ideal, and let $\widetilde J(\mathbb Q) =$ `eisensteinQuotientRational` be the image in $\widetilde J$ of those $x$ with $\sigma\cdot x - x$ in that submodule for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$. Assume the additive subgroup generated by $\widetilde J(\mathbb Q)$ is finitely generated, and set $M =$ `eisensteinQuotientRationalLocalized p q`, the localisation of the $\mathbb T$-span of $\widetilde J(\mathbb Q)$ at the complement of the prime `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q`, the contraction of $(q)$ along `eisensteinEval p`. Assume further that for every $m$ there is a Kummer row `JKummerRow q m M`: abelian groups $M^0, H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}, H^1$, an injection $M^0 \hookrightarrow M$ of finite index, $\delta \colon M^0 \to H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}$ with kernel $q^m M^0$, and $\mathrm{push} \colon H^1_{\mathrm{tors}} \to H^1$ exact after $\delta$ with image the $q^m$-torsion of $H^1$; and assume each $H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}$ is finite. Then there is $c_0 > 0$ with $[M : q^m M] \le c_0 \cdot \#H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}$ for all $m$, the index being that of the range of multiplication by $q^m$ on $M$.
--
--   This is the localised form of Mazur's counting step for the Eisenstein quotient: the index of $q^m M$ is bounded, uniformly in $m$, by the order of the Kummer target, with the constant absorbing the finite torsion of $M$. It feeds the proof that the rational points of the Eisenstein quotient form a torsion set, [`ModularCurve.eisensteinQuotientRational_isTorsion_heckeModuleBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eisensteinQuotientRational_isTorsion_heckeModuleBar).
